{"content_hash": "a8552699d904913e", "version_id": 733, "article_id": 74, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Christiane Amanpour leaves CNN after 43 years", "title_zh": "克里斯蒂安·阿曼普尔离开CNN，干了43年", "has_translation": true, "topic": "business", "source": "guardian_business", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/oct/19/christiane-amanpour-leaving-cnn", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1642723865493-9e4d57eca47a?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OXx8Y2hyaXN0aWFuZSUyMGFtYW5wb3VyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTI2Mjc2MzR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Eder Pozo Pérez on Unsplash", "author": "Eder Pozo Pérez", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@ederpozo?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-narrow-street-lined-with-buildings-and-flags-1FMCSwvV8F0?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(315, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(353, 46%, 48%)", "label": "BUSINESS", "seed": "937b1a603b6f"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-22", "word_count": 173, "reading_minutes": 0.9, "lead": "Christiane Amanpour is one of CNN's most famous journalists. On Monday, she said she will leave the network after 43 years. Her show will end in May, and she will leave at the end of June.", "lead_zh": "克里斯蒂安·阿曼普尔是CNN最有名的记者之一。周一她表示，自己将在工作43年后离开这家电视台。她的节目将在5月停播，她本人则在6月底离职。", "preview": "Amanpour started at CNN in 1983 as an assistant, when the network was still young. She later became its chief international anchor. In her s", "preview_zh": "阿曼普尔1983年进入CNN，当时这家电视台还很年轻，她做的是助理。后来她成为首席国际主播。在声明中她说，这个决定是经过好几个月思考、几个不眠之夜后做出的。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 721, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 65.45, "size_bytes": 393696, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 199, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 66.75, "size_bytes": 401472, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 199, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 71.425, "size_bytes": 429552, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 199, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 61.65, "size_bytes": 370800, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 199, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/74/en_b1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 67.25, "size_bytes": 404496, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 199, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/74/en_b1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@dcbf67c/content/data/versions/733.json", "paragraphs": ["Amanpour started at CNN in 1983 as an assistant, when the network was still young. She later became its chief international anchor. In her statement, she said she made the decision after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights.", "She reported on many major events, including the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, because they always worked hard to find the facts and broadcast the truth without fear or favor.", "Her departure comes at an important time, because CNN is now part of Skydance, a larger media company run by David Ellison. Her exit is not thought to be linked to the new owner, although some CNN journalists are worried about its closeness to the Trump administration.", "Amanpour, 68, has been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer since 2021. She will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to new projects. CNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship."], "paragraphs_zh": ["阿曼普尔1983年进入CNN，当时这家电视台还很年轻，她做的是助理。后来她成为首席国际主播。在声明中她说，这个决定是经过好几个月思考、几个不眠之夜后做出的。", "她报道过许多重大事件，包括第一次海湾战争、波黑战争、卢旺达、阿富汗、乌克兰和伊朗。她说，最重要的其实是团队和情谊，因为他们一直努力寻找事实，不畏不偏地播出真相。", "她的离开正值一个关键时刻，因为CNN现在属于Skydance这家更大的媒体公司，由大卫·埃里森经营。人们认为她的离职和新东家没有直接关系，不过一些CNN记者担心该公司与特朗普政府走得太近。", "68岁的阿曼普尔一直公开谈论自己从2021年起治疗卵巢癌。她将继续主持自己的播客，并期待新的项目。CNN首席执行官马克·汤普森感谢她43年来出色的新闻报道、忠诚和友谊。"], "body": "Amanpour started at CNN in 1983 as an assistant, when the network was still young. She later became its chief international anchor. In her statement, she said she made the decision after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights.\n\nShe reported on many major events, including the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, because they always worked hard to find the facts and broadcast the truth without fear or favor.\n\nHer departure comes at an important time, because CNN is now part of Skydance, a larger media company run by David Ellison. Her exit is not thought to be linked to the new owner, although some CNN journalists are worried about its closeness to the Trump administration.\n\nAmanpour, 68, has been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer since 2021. She will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to new projects. CNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship.", "body_zh": "阿曼普尔1983年进入CNN，当时这家电视台还很年轻，她做的是助理。后来她成为首席国际主播。在声明中她说，这个决定是经过好几个月思考、几个不眠之夜后做出的。\n\n她报道过许多重大事件，包括第一次海湾战争、波黑战争、卢旺达、阿富汗、乌克兰和伊朗。她说，最重要的其实是团队和情谊，因为他们一直努力寻找事实，不畏不偏地播出真相。\n\n她的离开正值一个关键时刻，因为CNN现在属于Skydance这家更大的媒体公司，由大卫·埃里森经营。人们认为她的离职和新东家没有直接关系，不过一些CNN记者担心该公司与特朗普政府走得太近。\n\n68岁的阿曼普尔一直公开谈论自己从2021年起治疗卵巢癌。她将继续主持自己的播客，并期待新的项目。CNN首席执行官马克·汤普森感谢她43年来出色的新闻报道、忠诚和友谊。", "text": "Amanpour started at CNN in 1983 as an assistant, when the network was still young. She later became its chief international anchor. In her statement, she said she made the decision after many months of thought and a few sleepless nights. She reported on many major events, including the first Gulf war, the Bosnian war, Rwanda, Afghanistan, Ukraine and Iran. She said the teams and the friendship mattered most, because they always worked hard to find the facts and broadcast the truth without fear or favor. Her departure comes at an important time, because CNN is now part of Skydance, a larger media company run by David Ellison. Her exit is not thought to be linked to the new owner, although some CNN journalists are worried about its closeness to the Trump administration. Amanpour, 68, has been open about her treatment for ovarian cancer since 2021. She will keep hosting her podcast and looks forward to new projects. CNN's CEO, Mark Thompson, thanked her for 43 extraordinary years of journalism, loyalty and friendship.", "vocab": [{"word": "anchor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "主播", "note": "新闻节目主持人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "network", "pos": "noun", "zh": "电视网；电视台", "note": "常指大型媒体机构", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "statement", "pos": "noun", "zh": "声明", "note": "公开表态", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "assignment", "pos": "noun", "zh": "任务；报道任务", "note": "记者出外采访的工作", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "camaraderie", "pos": "noun", "zh": "同志情谊", "note": "团队之间的友好感情", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "broadcast", "pos": "verb", "zh": "播出", "note": "也可作名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "departure", "pos": "noun", "zh": "离开；离职", "note": "depart 的名词形式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}